  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song-dance of far-western Nepal (Sudurpashchim and parts of Karnali), sung in Doteli and neighbouring dialects at festivals such as Gaura and at village fairs. Participants hold hands in a circle and step together while two sides trade improvised couplets, often as courtship or teasing dialogue. The circle is often sung without instruments, carried by the dancers' steps; Radio Nepal broadcasts and commercial deuda albums add madal and other accompaniment.",
